    "https://www.martin.edu/programsandservices": {
      "title": "Bursar",
      "description": "PROGRAMS AND SERVICES | Martin University | Indianapolis | Higher Education top of page Bursar Bursar (317) 543-3235 DONATE ACCREDITATION ABOUT Mission/Vision/Values History FAQ Facility Rental Human Resources GIVE ADMISSIONS Returning Students Financial Aid Bursar Plan A Visit Contact Us Consumer Information ACADEMICS Academic Advising School of Education Undergraduate Programs Stackable Credential & Certificates Graduate Programs Master of Organizational Leadership Returning Students International Students Registrar Faculty Academic Calendar Institutional Research and Effectiveness MU GLOBAL CAMPUS MARTIN WORKS Job Ready Badging Program MY MARTIN Student Services Student Disability Services Alumni Association Career Resource Center My Martin Portal Martin U Merchandise NEWS & EVENTS Martin Insider Podcast Media Campus Alerts Internet Offering Use tab to navigate through the menu items. No Inclement Weather Alerts Meet Our Team Martin WORKS Alumni Connection The P.A.C.E Center The P.A.C.E Center provides programs, services, and events students can connect with that will help them to achieve their professional goals and engage in experiential learning. We will explore Active Career Exploration, Solid On Job Experiences, Reflective Observation, Conceptualization of Smart Goals, and Documented and Sharable Soft Skill Assessments through state-approved Job Badges. Overview Martin WORKS Academy Career Counseling Online Job Search: Handshake Job Opportunities Interview prep/Mock Interviews Professional Development Networking Opportunities 9 CORE Career Readiness Competencies Equity & Inclusion Leadership Financial Literacy Critical Thinking Teamwork Technology Professional Communication Career & Self Development Programs & Events Career Pathways Careers Event Calendar Career Development Resources Career Development Resources is excited to connect you to our Dress For Success Virtual Closet for women in addition to donating gently used Men’s clothing to www.careergear.org which provides students access to FREE professional attire appropriate for career fairs, interviews, networking events and the workplace. Handshake is a job-ready platform Martin University uses to connect students to early-in-career internships, part-time, and full-time jobs in Indiana. They partner with hundreds of Indiana employers and are completely free for you to use. To access the Network and receive personalized role suggestions, activate your account  and sign up for an initial meeting with a Career Resource Specialist. ​ Activate your account Apprenticeship Employment Guide Explore Guide Common Interview Questions Download PDF Dress for Success Women’s Apparel Business Suits Separates: Skirts, Blazers, Dresses, and Slacks Tops: Dress Blouses and Button Up Shirts Shoes and Accessories: Pumps (1-3\" heels,) Belts, Jewelry, and Hosiery (new) Visit Website Success Wear Men’s Apparel Business Suits Separates: Suit Jackets and Dress Pants Tops: Long Sleeve Dress Shirts Shoes and Accessories: Dress Shoes, Ties, Belts, and Dress/ Trouser Socks Learn More Program Partners We Welcome Donations Career Development Services welcomes donations of new and clean, gently worn business attire to help ensure that our students make a strong first impression. Thank you, in advance, for your support! All donations are tax-deductible to the extent provided by law. Please follow the link https://www.indydfs.org. If you have questions, feel free to contact  the Career Development Resource Center. Staff Office of Career Development Staff Sydney H. Burt, M.Ed. Vice President of Enrollment, Career Services, and Student Success Phone: (317) 917-3343 Email: sburt@martin.edu Home ​ About Martin University Mission Leadership History FAQs Accreditation Facility Rental Human Resources COVID-19 Polic y Inclement Weather Alert Admissions How To Apply Financial Aid Bursar Consumer Information Plan A Visit Contact Us Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Department Of Students Services Prior Learning Assessment (PLA) Registrar Academic Calendar Do Not Sell My Personal Information My Martin Alumni Association My Martin News & Events Media Campus Alerts MARTIN NEWSLETTER Martin University 2186 North Sherman Drive, Indianapolis, IN 46218 ​ Phone ( 317) 917-3966 ​ Fax (317) 917-3393 ​ Administrative B uilding Hours: Monday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Tuesday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Wednesday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Thursday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Saturday Closed Sunday Closed Career Opportunities | Donate | Request A Transcript | Contact An Enrollment Advisor | Higher Education Opportunity Act bottom of page"
