      "title": "Bursar",
      "description": "Human Resources | Martin University | Indianapolis top of page Bursar Bursar (317) 543-3235 DONATE ACCREDITATION ABOUT Mission/Vision/Values History FAQ Facility Rental Human Resources GIVE ADMISSIONS Returning Students Financial Aid Bursar Plan A Visit Contact Us Consumer Information ACADEMICS Academic Advising School of Education Undergraduate Programs Stackable Credential & Certificates Graduate Programs Master of Organizational Leadership Returning Students International Students Registrar Faculty Academic Calendar Institutional Research and Effectiveness MU GLOBAL CAMPUS MARTIN WORKS Job Ready Badging Program MY MARTIN Student Services Student Disability Services Alumni Association Career Resource Center My Martin Portal Martin U Merchandise NEWS & EVENTS Martin Insider Podcast Media Campus Alerts Internet Offering Use tab to navigate through the menu items. No Inclement Weather Alerts Office of Human Resources Functions: Human Resource Management Organizational Design & Policy Classification & Compensation Recruitment & Selection Performance Management Employee Benefits Training & Development Employee Relations Contact hresources@martin.edu Phone: 317.543.3672 ​ Equal Opportunity Employment: Martin University provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, amnesty or status as a covered veteran in accordance with applicable Federal, State and Local laws. E-VERIFY Notices Participation Notice – English/Spanish Career Opportunities Career Opportunities Martin University currently has the following career opportunities available. Click on the open positions below for additional information. ​ Interested in becoming an Adjunct Professor, submit your resume by clicking here . MU Compliance Martin University Compliance The role of Martin University's Compliance Department is to provide regulatory compliance to support the mission of Martin University and to enhance the educational environment and service to its faculty, staff and students. To Report A Concern Anonymously Call – Compliance Hotline: 317 917-3394 Contact compliance@martin.edu Phone: 317.543.3672 REPORT A CONCERN Martin University encourages everyone to be proactive in preventing noncompliant activities by reporting/disclosing acts that you reasonably believe may violate the law or University's policies to an appropriate University official. To report a concern or to request assistance in identifying a concern, contact the Director of Compliance. If you do not feel comfortable reporting a concern or issue of wrongful conduct, you may submit a report anonymously. NON-RETALIATION Retaliation against any employee or student who has submitted a complaint or concern in good is faith is strictly prohibited.  Those who submit good faith reports or inquires are entitled to be treated in accordance with whitsleblower protections outlined in the Indiana State Statutes. TRANSPARENCY IN COVERAGE Through UnitedHealthcare, UMR and HealthSCOPE Benefits creates and publishes the Machine-Readable Files on behalf of Martin University. ​ To link to the Machine-Readable Files, please click on the URL provided: transparency-in-coverage.uhc.com Home ​ About Martin University Mission Leadership History FAQs Accreditation Facility Rental Human Resources COVID-19 Polic y Inclement Weather Alert Admissions How To Apply Financial Aid Bursar Consumer Information Plan A Visit Contact Us Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Department Of Students Services Prior Learning Assessment (PLA) Registrar Academic Calendar Do Not Sell My Personal Information My Martin Alumni Association My Martin News & Events Media Campus Alerts MARTIN NEWSLETTER Martin University 2186 North Sherman Drive, Indianapolis, IN 46218 ​ Phone ( 317) 917-3966 ​ Fax (317) 917-3393 ​ Administrative B uilding Hours: Monday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Tuesday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Wednesday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Thursday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Saturday Closed Sunday Closed Career Opportunities | Donate | Request A Transcript | Contact An Enrollment Advisor | Higher Education Opportunity Act bottom of page"
